  "generated_text": "1. A regular dodecagon has 12 vertices.\n2. To form a triangle, we need to choose 3 vertices out of these 12.\n3. The number of ways to choose 3 vertices from 12 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of items, and \\( k \\) is the number of items to choose.\n4. Here, \\( n = 12 \\) and \\( k = 3 \\).\n\n\\[\n\\binom{12}{3} = \\frac{12!}{3!(12-3)!} = \\frac{12!}{3! \\cdot 9!}\n\\]\n\n5. Simplify the factorials:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{12}{3} = \\frac{12 \\times 11 \\times 10}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{1320}{6} = 220\n\\]\n\nSo, the total number of triangles that can be formed using the vertices of a regular dodecagon is \\(\\boxed{220}\\).",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[220, '220']",
    "gold_answer": "No three vertices are collinear, so any combination of 3 vertices will make a triangle. Choosing 3 out of 12 is $\\binom{12}{3}=\\boxed{220}.$",
    "is_correct": true
  },
